Package: evbsreg
Type: Package
Title: Local Influence Diagnostics for the Extreme-Value
        Birnbaum-Saunders Regression Model
Version: 1.2.3
Date: 2026-10-23
Authors@R: 
    person("Raydonal", "Ospina",
           email = "raydonal@de.ufpe.br",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9884-9090"))
Description: Local influence diagnostics for the Extreme-Value
    Birnbaum-Saunders (EVBS) regression model of Ferreira, Gomes and Leiva
    (2012): joint maximum likelihood estimation, conformal normal curvature
    diagnostics under case-weight, response and explanatory-variable
    perturbation, randomized quantile residuals with simulation envelope, the
    density, distribution and quantile functions, the finite upper endpoint,
    return levels and expected shortfall, moving-block bootstrap standard
    errors, a prospective index of endpoint identifiability, the same
    diagnostics for generalized extreme-value regression, and a 'gamlss'
    family allowing the tail-shape parameter to depend on covariates. The
    methods are described in Lima, Ospina, Barros and Macedo (2025)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2507.22967> and are applied to monthly maximum wind
    gusts from Itajai, Brazil.
